The change wraps the `yield` in `try/finally` in `_FieldNameStack.push` and `_ModelTypeStack.push`, so the stack is popped even when schema generation raises. That is correct. The two new tests cover both stacks.

F1 and F2 do not look like real failures. The two tests belong to the counter and ordered-dict schemas added in earlier commits, not to this diff. Their test IDs include object memory addresses (`0xffffb2117230`), which change on every run. That makes the same tests look new at head and explains why 45 tests appear removed (F3). The 47 added tests are probably those 45 re-addressed IDs plus the 2 new tests.
